WEBVTT

00:00:00.102 --> 00:00:03.349
Before we start writing code I want to connect this
module to

00:00:03.375 --> 00:00:09.815
what we already learned In Module 4 we summarized
rows We

00:00:09.841 --> 00:00:16.336
counted records calculated averages grouped data and
created analytical summaries Module

00:00:16.362 --> 00:00:20.911
5 is different Now we are asking SQL to make
decisions about

00:00:20.924 --> 00:00:26.181
individual values and records For example should
this patient be included in

00:00:26.207 --> 00:00:31.903
a report Is this billing record considered high
value Does this patient

00:00:31.929 --> 00:00:36.143
have a usable contact method What should happen when
a value is

00:00:36.168 --> 00:00:40.189
missing A good habit is to first explain the rule in
normal

00:00:40.215 --> 00:00:46.452
language Then break that rule into smaller
conditions After that translate

00:00:46.478 --> 00:00:51.143
those conditions into SQL We will also test edge
cases because a

00:00:51.168 --> 00:00:54.145
query can run successfully and still give the wrong
answer
